{"title":"Career roadmap · Exhibition Manager","role":"Exhibition Manager","summary":"An Exhibition Manager plans, coordinates and delivers exhibitions, trade shows, expos, conferences and large-scale public or commercial events. The role combines event operations, venue management, exhibitor relations, sponsorship, sales, marketing, budgeting, logistics, visitor experience and on-site execution.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"BHM / B.Sc Hospitality & Hotel Administration / BTTM – Event Management"},"about":[{"label":"Core capabilities","text":"Event planning, exhibitor management, venue operations, logistics, budgeting, sponsorship, marketing and stakeholder coordination"},{"label":"Typical employers","text":"Event companies, exhibition organisers, convention centres, trade associations, hotels, convention bureaus, media companies and corporate event teams"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build event-management, hospitality, marketing and operations skills and complete live-event internships"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Progress from Event/Exhibition Executive or Coordinator toward Exhibition Manager"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Manage larger exhibitions, venues, exhibitors, sponsors and budgets"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Progress toward Exhibition Director, Event Director, Portfolio Director or independent event entrepreneur"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a student pursuing BHM / B.Sc Hospitality & Hotel Administration / BTTM with Event Management, Exhibition Management is a strong and direct career pathway."},{"type":"p","text":"The student should understand that an Exhibition Manager is usually not a first job after graduation. Most professionals begin as Event Executive, Exhibition Coordinator, Event Operations Executive, Exhibitor Services Executive or Conference/Event Associate and progress into management after gaining hands-on experience."},{"type":"p","text":"A typical progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Event Intern","Event/Exhibition Executive","Exhibition Coordinator","Exhibition Manager","Senior Exhibition Manager","Event Director / Exhibition Director"]}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong/direct alignment."},{"type":"p","text":"Event Management gives the student a relevant foundation. To reach Exhibition Manager level, add:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exhibition operations"},{"text":"MICE management"},{"text":"Venue management"},{"text":"Exhibitor acquisition"},{"text":"Sponsorship"},{"text":"B2B sales"},{"text":"Event marketing"},{"text":"Budgeting"},{"text":"Vendor management"},{"text":"Technology"},{"text":"Risk and safety"},{"text":"Data-driven event analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Timeline assumption"},{"type":"p","text":"This roadmap assumes a 3–4 year undergraduate programme beginning in 2026, depending on the institution. The final year should focus heavily on event internships, live-event exposure and professional portfolio development."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Event fundamentals, hospitality, communication and teamwork"},{"text":"College + event case studies"},{"text":"Event concept"},{"text":"Foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Event planning, budgeting and vendor coordination"},{"text":"Practical assignments"},{"text":"Mini-event plan"},{"text":"Planning"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Exhibition operations, venue management and floor planning"},{"text":"Live events + industry resources"},{"text":"Exhibition floor plan"},{"text":"Operations"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Marketing, sponsorship, sales and exhibitor management"},{"text":"Event projects"},{"text":"Sponsorship proposal"},{"text":"Commercial skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"MICE, B2B exhibitions, technology and analytics"},{"text":"Industry exposure"},{"text":"Exhibition business plan"},{"text":"Professional capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Live exhibition/event internship"},{"text":"Event organiser/venue"},{"text":"Event execution experience"},{"text":"Industry readiness"}],[{"text":"Final Year Sem 1"},{"text":"Leadership, contracts, risk, sustainability and large-event planning"},{"text":"Advanced projects"},{"text":"Full exhibition proposal"},{"text":"Management"}],[{"text":"Final Year Sem 2"},{"text":"Placement + portfolio + professional networking"},{"text":"Industry + mock interviews"},{"text":"Event portfolio"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Exhibition Manager skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Event management fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Event lifecycle"},{"text":"Event objectives"},{"text":"Event concept"},{"text":"Event planning"},{"text":"Event budgeting"},{"text":"Event timelines"},{"text":"Event operations"},{"text":"Event evaluation"},{"text":"Post-event reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Basic lifecycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Concept","Feasibility","Budget","Venue","Exhibitors/Sponsors","Marketing","Logistics","Build-up","Event","Dismantling","Evaluation"]}]},{"heading":"Exhibition management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exhibition concept development"},{"text":"Floor planning"},{"text":"Booth allocation"},{"text":"Exhibitor onboarding"},{"text":"Exhibitor manuals"},{"text":"Stall specifications"},{"text":"Registration"},{"text":"Visitor management"},{"text":"Contractor coordination"},{"text":"Move-in/move-out"},{"text":"On-site operations"},{"text":"Dismantling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understa